93rrKwlUnSM	https://unsplash.com/photos/93rrKwlUnSM	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1532727812519-93f8248c35da	2018-07-27 21:49:58.772182	t	3245	4867	0.67000000000000004	I will always remember this hike. For our honeymoon, my wife and I traveled to Olympic National Park in the Pacific Northwest. The fog beautifully wrapped the rainforest-like woods and added to the moody feel. It seemed like we saw every shade of green and grey that day as we hiked through the hills along a small stream. I’ll never forget the feeling, taking in those beautiful sights with my wife on our first trip together as a married couple.	iam_aspencer	Andrew	Spencer	Canon	Canon EOS REBEL T3i	400	6.3	70.0	1/800	Olympic National Park, Port Angeles, United States	47.8021067	-123.6043524	United States	Port Angeles	1431993	6156	top view of forest					LA8E6zof009Z~qt7D%IUIUxuxuM{
nhlvWBVicTg	https://unsplash.com/photos/nhlvWBVicTg	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1531524197082-8ac02ebb64a9	2018-07-13 23:31:45.349929	t	3378	2370	1.4299999999999999	A painting of a cosy stone cottage by Sian Butler (my Mum). Sian is well known for her Australian Outback pastel paintings (number one, two, three etc., on Australian Google image search), but she is a also very versatile artist and has done a series of acrylic paintings of cottages. They are mostly inspired by cottages in Tasmania, but with an obvious British influence. In her cottage series, I like the way Sian has combined numerous textures and techniques to produce delightful scenes. She wants you to enjoy them and share them.	davidclode	David	Clode	Canon	Canon PowerShot SX700 HS	125	4.0	4.5	1/1250	Tasmania, Australia	-41.4545196	145.9706647	Australia		1323967	6063	painting og brown and blue wooden door and shingle wall					LCF$FeOs#i$HXgNZo4T0}*nNRWNh
