Iem8O6y7ErA	https://unsplash.com/photos/Iem8O6y7ErA	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513479965714-5cefd1d34303	2017-12-17 03:10:21.46594	t	5184	3456	1.5	Driving along the Atlantic Coast, we stumbled across the roof of a building peering out of the sand. Nambia’s coast used to have a number of whaling stations - but when the business was not profitable - the buildings were abandoned and left to rot. In beautiful irony, nature reclaimed the land from where the stations stood. And as I stood on the roof of the building I stared down into the now empty expanse and appreciated the unforgiving nature of the landscape around me.	chinkinthearmour	Ryan	Cheng	Canon	Canon EOS 650D	100	16.0	39.0	1/100	Sandwich Harbour Historic, Namibia	-23.3500832	14.502853	Namibia		1284671	6219	sand dunes					LZNIpjenR*ay.TRjj[j[yrofWBa|
