5L47XYRvGOo	https://unsplash.com/photos/5L47XYRvGOo	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1547409706-33cc240a1f5e	2019-01-13 20:02:01.944706	t	5472	3078	1.78	"The Dugongs of Marsha Shouna (Dugong dugon)    Dugongs are believed to be inspirations behind tales of mermaids and in parts of Indonesia they are considered reincarnations of women. The word ""dugong"" means lady of the sea. It's herbivorous and feed uniquely on sea grass. Their numbers are very low and in some countries they are entirely depleted due to hunting, bycatch and habitat destruction. I was extremely lucky to encounter one in Marsha Shouna on the western coast of the Red Sea, once home to thousands of dugongs but now with very few individuals. The 100 km coastline along Marsa Alam had only seven dugongs left at the time of writing."	kmkr	Kris-Mikael	Krister	SONY	DSC-RX100	125	5.6	10.4	1/250						884884	5151	beige sea creature underwater photography					LRDS?$rX1INatSozIpRjXTRkVtxZ
