yq8c6k5fBnQ	https://unsplash.com/photos/yq8c6k5fBnQ	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1542961996-3f032eec02cb	2018-11-23 08:33:30.049147	t	2272	3404	0.67000000000000004	The Longest ‘Blood Moon’ Eclipse of the Century.    A lunar eclipse occurs when the Earth passes between the sun and the moon.  Unlike with a solar eclipse, when the moon passes between the Earth and sun, blocking the sun’s light, the moon is not “turned dark” during an eclipse, but instead appears to turn red.    Because there is light scattered through the atmosphere of the Earth, some of the sun’s light gets bounced around the edge of the Earth to hit the moon.    Blue and violet wavelengths are scattered more than red and orange ones, this making the moon appear red.	luxdamore	🐣 Luca	Iaconelli 🦊	RICOH IMAGING COMPANY, LTD.	PENTAX K-1	1600	5.6	105.0	8	Via Errano, 20, 48018 Faenza RA, Italy, Faenza	44.26715333	11.82553	Italy	Faenza	8185586	60737	view of red moon					L01e-3of1Kj[RiWBWVay1hof}Xf8
