3pekyY0-yOw	https://unsplash.com/photos/3pekyY0-yOw	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1541707519942-08fd2f6480ba	2018-11-08 20:21:11.422184	t	4928	3264	1.51	On a family trip to the Sanbona Nature Reserve we came across a pair of cheetahs who were just waking up as the sun was setting.  I was able to get close enough to them to take a number of pictures of this one who was sitting up a few yards away from his dozing brother.  The evening sun was coming from the side and the light was such that the mountains behind turned a dark blue, forming a perfect backdrop.  Sanbona is about 4 hours’ drive from Cape Town in the scrubland semi-desert of the Karoo - which explains the heather-like plants that can be seen in the picture.	bird_mike	Mike	Bird	NIKON CORPORATION	NIKON D7000	100	6.3	300.0	1/250						645668	5205	leopard sitting on grass field					LGB:suV[0Mt6b}t3t3ja?HxYxsNH
