0QZOCgk10w4	https://unsplash.com/photos/0QZOCgk10w4	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1542372781736-b2085952aa8c	2018-11-16 12:59:46.868459	t	3133	2350	1.3300000000000001	Sometimes you can’t control your environment. Some photographers prefer to shoot in studios for this reason; it gives them the power to decide every single aspect of the image they’re creating. In my opinion, there is something beautiful about working alongside nature to create images that express something deeper: the relationship between people and the earth.     Who needs expensive lights and studios when you have the beauty of the outdoors that gives something new every time? The wind that caused my model’s hair to react that way was completely unplanned, but it’s what made this photo.	jakewxlker	Jake	Walker	Canon	Canon EOS 5D Mark II	100	2.8	24.0	1/800	Switzerland	46.818188	8.22751199999993	Switzerland		1123488	4181	woman in white collared top					LZHV9wkCtlof~qWBxvt7?ct7M_ay
