J2f1PriKFEg	https://unsplash.com/photos/J2f1PriKFEg	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1533206831064-decd0fb382a0	2018-08-02 10:48:21.738992	t	14007	8801	1.5900000000000001	Like so most glaciers around the world, the Griesgletscher is rapidly declining in length while also deflating like a giant balloon. It is incredible that change is happening so quickly and shows what may well come in only a few more years. I post this not to instill fear but rather to show that things must change if we humans are interested in living well in the future. Indeed, we can choose to live indoors. However, the destruction of the natural world and its beauty is a tragedy. Life will always go on… but perhaps without humans enjoying the smell of fresh air in the mountains.	martinadams	Martin	Adams	Canon	Canon EOS 80D	100	8.0	100.0	1/400	Griessee, Obergoms, Switzerland	46.4588629783102	8.36343242905275	Switzerland	Obergoms	3035745	11760	landscape of mountain covered with snow					LiI#.JD%ITtR~WMxkCax%~bbV@of
