s48nn4NtlZ4	https://unsplash.com/photos/s48nn4NtlZ4	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1476824236633-95c4f45583a3	2016-10-18 20:58:06.039747	t	6000	3255	1.8400000000000001	One of the reasons why I go camping is because something unexpected always happens, and with minimal amenities at your disposal, you are forced to adapt and find a way to enjoy your experience. This night, it was an unexpected storm blowing into the valley. My girlfriend and I positioned the car to block the wind, and made a big fire to keep us warm. Stoking the fire, we noticed the wind was blowing embers across the ground inviting us to take a unique long exposure image. This photo is the result of making the best out of a bad situation, and a reminder of why I love camping.	robsonhmorgan	Robson Hatsukami	Morgan	SONY	ILCE-7	1600			2.5	Trona Pinnacles, United States	35.617736	-117.3681094	United States		2341260	11726	person sitting beside car under cloudy sky					LTEK+JV@0zbb5Us:$yWB5USg-Rn$
